// Change: update to existing rule
// Title: Potential WSL InstallLocation Registry Key Modification
// Sigma ID: 83475063-b1c8-4774-9568-69bbda71a539
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Liran Ravich, Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-05-05 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: stealth, defense-impairment, persistence, T1112, T1218
// Description: Detects modifications to the Windows Subsystem for Linux (WSL) InstallLocation registry key.
//   Attackers can modify this registry key to redirect the execution flow of legitimate WSL
//   processes (wsl.exe or bash.exe) to a malicious payload, acting as a proxy execution and defense
//   evasion technique.
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - https://web.archive.org/web/20260718025639/https://cardinalops.com/blog/bash-and-switch-hijacking-via-windows-subsystem-for-linux/
//   - https://blog.qualys.com/vulnerabilities-threat-research/2022/04/20/implications-of-windows-subsystem-for-linux-for-adversaries-defenders-part-2
//   - https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/news/security/new-malware-uses-windows-subsystem-for-linux-for-stealthy-attacks/
//   - https://thehackernews.com/2021/09/new-malware-targets-windows-subsystem.html
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/wsl/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/3b26628c02b9f77741b6f068e9ce40a87740d455/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_wsl_installlocation_registry_key_modification.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey contains "\\Lxss\\MSI\\InstallLocation" and (not((((RegistryValueData in~ ("C:\\Program Files\\WSL", "%ProgramFiles%\\WSL")) or (RegistryValueData contains ":\\Program Files\\WindowsApps\\MicrosoftCorporationII.WindowsSubsystemForLinux_" or RegistryValueData contains "\\AppData\\Local\\Microsoft\\WindowsApps" or RegistryValueData contains "%ProgramFiles%\\WindowsApps\\MicrosoftCorporationII.WindowsSubsystemForLinux_")) or (InitiatingProcessFolderPath in~ ("C:\\Windows\\System32\\msiexec.exe", "C:\\Windows\\SysWOW64\\msiexec.exe")))))
